---
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "@/config/site";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | 559 Solutions"
  description="Privacy information for the 559 Solutions website, including forms, newsletters, analytics, external services, and cookies."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy Policy" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Site information</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">How this site is intended to handle information.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="narrow legal-content">
      <p><strong>Draft last updated:</strong> November 5, 2026</p>
      <p>
        This draft describes the planned data practices for 559 Solutions. It is not a legal guarantee and must be reviewed before production launch.
      </p>

      <h2>Information submitted through forms</h2>
      <p>
        Contact and lead-magnet forms may collect the information shown on the form, such as a name, email address, organization, inquiry type, and message. Submissions are sent to a Google Apps Script web app in the 559 Solutions Google Workspace account, which records them in a Google Sheet. Google processes this information under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletters and lead magnets</h2>
      <p>
        If you sign up for email, 559 Solutions records your email address, the page you signed up from, and your consent in the same Google Sheet. It is used only to send the emails described on the form. To stop, reply to any email or use the contact form.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics are disabled by default. If analytics are enabled, this policy must identify the provider, the information collected, the retention approach, and any available opt-out method.
      </p>

      <h2>Checkout, scheduling, and embedded services</h2>
      <p>
        Product checkout, scheduling, video, and other embedded services may operate under their own terms and privacy policies. Each service in use is named on the page where it appears.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The first release does not require nonessential cookies. A consent banner should be added only if enabled services make it necessary.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and retention</h2>
      <p>
        The site collects only the information needed for the stated purpose. Form submissions are stored with the form provider, not in the website files, and are kept only as long as they are needed to respond.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy or your information, email <a href={`mailto:${site.publicEmail}`}>{site.publicEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
